{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he divided.</b> He cut them and separated them. Like it: על הרי בתר (Song of Songs 2:17), בין בתריו (Jeremiah 34:18)." "<b>And he set each piece.</b> Know that the word איש is like בעל. So too איש מלחמה (Exodus 15:3), והאיש גבריאל (Daniel 9:21). And the meaning of בעל is the essence of the thing; so too איש בליעל (II Samuel 22:20, I Samuel 25:25), construct state also for animals and curtains: אשה אל אחותה (Exodus 26:3). He set each piece opposite its fellow, for the beast and the man are two." "<b>The bird he did not divide.</b> The turtledove and the young pigeon, for צפור is a general term."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "The citations איש בליעל are given as (ש\"ב, כ, א); resolved to II Samuel 22:20 by inference among standard prooftexts for this phrase, but the chapter/verse is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:42.100853324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}